# HTML → Kadence Conversion Framework

When the user supplies HTML to convert into Kadence blocks:

1. Read `.cursor/html-to-kadence/project.yaml` — **required**
2. Read `.cursor/workflows/html-to-kadence-pipeline.md`
3. Read `docs/kadence-html-mapping.md`
4. Read `.cursor/docs/kadence-markup-validation.md` — **mandatory**
5. Load skill `html-to-kadence` from `~/.cursor/skills/html-to-kadence/SKILL.md`

## Core agents (run in order)

| Step | Agent | Skill |
|------|-------|-------|
| 1–6 | Kadence Architect | `.cursor/skills/kadence-architect/SKILL.md` |
| 7–8 | Design System Extractor | `.cursor/skills/design-system-extractor/SKILL.md` |
| 9 | HTML Analyzer | `.cursor/skills/html-analyzer/SKILL.md` |
| 10 | Pattern Finder | `.cursor/skills/pattern-finder/SKILL.md` |
| 11–12 | Kadence Block Composer | `.cursor/skills/kadence-block-composer/SKILL.md` |
| 13–16 | QA Reviewer | `.cursor/skills/qa-reviewer/SKILL.md` |
| 17 | REST Publisher | `.cursor/skills/rest-publisher/SKILL.md` |

## Non-negotiables

- Read `project.yaml` → `learnings` before every conversion
- Clone from `pages.clone_source` — do not invent block JSON
- Native Kadence blocks only (see `conversion.allow_custom_html`)
- Never publish unless user explicitly requests
- `GET` current page content before any `PUT` that replaces `content`

## Outputs

1. Block markup (`<!-- wp:kadence/... -->`)
2. Conversion report (mapping, tokens, QA summary)
3. Optional publish report
